[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-198b6a3e-57b0-463f-981b-d2e5041be6db\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Track</p><strong>Thu 1 May 2025 11:45 - 12:00 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/icse-2025/icse-2025-venue-206-plus-208\" class=\"room-link navigate\">206 plus 208</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2025/icse-2025-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">Human and Social 2</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/aserebrenik\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Alexander Serebrenik</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"198b6a3e-57b0-463f-981b-d2e5041be6db\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>How Scientists Use Jupyter Notebooks: Goals, Quality Attributes, and Opportunities</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><span class=\"pull-right\"><span title=\"Artifact-Functional - The Artifact Evaluation Track has assessed this paper to have an artifact that is functional.\" class=\"output-badge\"><img alt=\"Artifact-Functional\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getImageFile/1684d5c8-60b5-4920-92a7-29f5166bdbac/small?1742858829000\" class=\"outputimage\"/></span></span><span class=\"pull-right\"><span title=\"Artifact-Available - The Artifact Evaluation Track has assessed this paper to have an available artifact.\" class=\"output-badge\"><img alt=\"Artifact-Available\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getImageFile/7a1a017a-f54b-452f-8ba0-242f91498ef0/small?1742858953000\" class=\"outputimage\"/></span></span><span class=\"pull-right\"><span title=\"Artifact-Reusable - The Artifact Evaluation Track has assessed this paper to have an artifact that is reusable.\" class=\"output-badge\"><img alt=\"Artifact-Reusable\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getImageFile/fdc6ea94-f3ec-4d36-9270-b88c7e8636dc/small?1742858695000\" class=\"outputimage\"/></span></span><p>Computational notebooks are intended to prioritize the needs of scientists, but little is known about how scientists interact with notebooks, what requirements drive scientists\u2019 software development processes, or what tactics scientists use to meet their requirements. We conducted an observational study of 20 scientists using Jupyter notebooks for their day-to-day tasks, finding that scientists prioritize different quality attributes depending on their goals. A qualitative analysis of their usage shows (1) a collection of goals scientists pursue with Jupyter notebooks, (2) a set of quality attributes that scientists value when they write software, and (3) tactics that scientists leverage to promote quality. In addition, we identify ways scientists incorporated AI tools into their notebook work. From our observations, we derive design recommendations for improving computational notebooks and future programming systems for scientists. Key opportunities pertain to helping scientists create and manage state, dependencies, and abstractions in their software, enabling more effective reuse of clearly-defined components.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.12309\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> Pre-print</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/ruanqianqianlisahuang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Ruanqianqian (Lisa) Huang\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/ruanqianqianlisahuang/9750e52c-b56d-4c9f-8136-2ee262240a00/micro-avatar?1783976324000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Ruanqianqian <span class=\"name-visual-sep\"></span>(Lisa) Huang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California, San Diego</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/savitharavi\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Savitha Ravi\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/savitharavi/54954f4e-a0d4-45dd-be44-e5273526a69c/micro-avatar?1783979266000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Savitha Ravi<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">UC San Diego</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/michaelhe\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Michael He<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">UCSD</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/boyutian\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Boyu Tian<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California, San Diego</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/sorinlerner\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Sorin Lerner\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/sorinlerner/76e2370c-74bb-4854-881c-84d2c3a8e239/micro-avatar?1783974147000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Sorin Lerner<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California at San Diego</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/michaelcoblenz\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Michael Coblenz\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/michaelcoblenz/5cf02c6e-08af-4ae2-9d7f-e4a1fdd20af5/micro-avatar?1783971767000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Michael Coblenz<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California, San Diego</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2025/icse-2025-research-track/201/How-Scientists-Use-Jupyter-Notebooks-Goals-Quality-Attributes-and-Opportunities\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default na